K0 [known answer] HT sector alone: L = sqrt(-g)(-2 Lambda) + 2 Lambda d_mu B^mu
  [OK ] K0a  B^mu equation is -2 d_mu Lambda = 0 (Lambda constant)
  [OK ] K0b  Lambda equation is d_mu B^mu = sqrt(-g) (unimodular volume)

E1-E2  with the tie: L = -2 sqrt(-g) J(Y, Lambda) + 2 Lambda d_mu B^mu, J generic
  [OK ] E1   B^mu equation unchanged by the tie: d_mu Lambda = 0 exactly, whatever J is
  [OK ] E2   Lambda equation: d_mu B^mu = sqrt(-g) dJ/dLambda|_Y  (fixes B only)

E3   dJ/dLambda at fixed Y
  [OK ] E3a  form G: J = Lambda j(Y/Lambda) gives dJ/dLambda = j - y j'(y), y = Y/Lambda
  [OK ] E3b  form U: dJ/dLambda = 1 - alpha^2 h(u), h(u) = 2(u - ln(1+u)) - u^2/(1+u)
  [OK ] E3c  h(u) = u^3/3 - u^4/2 + ... near u = 0
  [OK ] E3d  h(u) > 0 for u in [1e-3, 1e3] (61 log points)   (min h = 3.328e-10 at u = 1e-3)

K1 [known answer] v3s's J: 1 + J' = u/(1+u) (simple-mu static law), a0 = c^2 alpha sqrt(Lambda)
  [OK ] K1a  1 + dJ/dY = u/(1+u)
  [OK ] K1b  J(0; Lambda) = Lambda (the vacuum value the multiplier carries)

E4   at Lambda = const the remaining field equations are the parent's (stand-in field phi, Y = (d phi)^2)
  [OK ] E4   EL_phi[Lambda(x)] at Lambda(x) = Lambda0 minus EL_phi[Lambda0] = 0 (test configuration, 30 digits)   (|difference| = 3.4e-167)
  [OK ] E4b  the 2 Lambda d_mu B^mu term contains no metric (zero stress tensor)

E5   d det(g)/d g_ij = det(g) (g^-1)_ji, so -2 sqrt(-g) J(0) gives J(0) g_mu_nu = Lambda g_mu_nu in the metric equation
  [OK ] E5   Jacobi's formula on a general 4x4 matrix

S / G5   scale relation: kappa^2 = a0^2 / (c^2 G rho_Lambda,obs),  rho_Lambda,obs = Lambda_obs c^2/(8 pi G),  Lambda_obs = Lambda + Lambda_v
